<title>UK: Nat Express set to buy Scottish bus firm.</title>
<headline>Nat Express set to buy Scottish bus firm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bus and train operating group National Express Plc said on Thursday it had been selected as preferred bidder for Taybus Holdings Ltd, an operator of public transport buses based in Dundee, Scotland.</p>
<p>No financial details of the proposed deal were disclosed, but National Express said in a statement that Taybus had about 500 employees, a fleet of about 150 buses and turnover in the year to March 1996 of 12.3 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
